ant, for a constant consider making this a classproperty. also why make it all caps? no need to shout :p ", "createdAt": "2026-10-26T22:04:25Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/806#discussion_r4383030426"}, {"databaseId": 4385822160, "author": {"login": "AbdelrhmanBassiouny"}, "body": "This is an enum member", "createdAt": "2026-10-27T06:43:33Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/806#discussion_r4385822160"}]}}, {"id": "PRRT_kwDOQga1Oc6wfJ6S", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": false, "path": "krrood/src/krrood/development_tools/rules/python_rules.py", "line": 56, "comments": {"nodes": [{"databaseId": 4383393708, "author": {"login": "LucaKro"}, "body": "why not make those actual superclasses?", "createdAt": "2026-10-26T22:55:36Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/806#discussion_r4383393708"}, {"databaseId": 4385843291, "author": {"login": "AbdelrhmanBassiouny"}, "body": "That was the reason behind generic enumeration, these were the generic parameters. \r\n\r\nYou cannot in python subclass an enum that has members, and actually semantically this is more correct, as the relationship here is more a part-whole relationship than a subclass relationship, it is a subsection of that bigger existing section.\r\n\r\nSubclassing would mean that you also take the parent section rules as part of the subsection rules which is wrong. ", "createdAt": "2026-10-27T06:47:08Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/806#discussion_r4385843291"}]}}, {"id": "PRRT_kwDOQga1Oc6wodeu", "isResolved": false, "isOutdated": true, "path": "krrood/src/krrood/development_tools/rules/krrood_rules.py", "line": null, "comments": {"nodes": [{"databaseId": 4387310122, "author": {"login": "tomsch420"}, "body": "this is a very generic term for some very specific information about errors. Chose something more fitting", "createdAt": "2026-10-27T09:59:50Z", "url":