9, "comments": {"nodes": [{"databaseId": 4391885993, "author": {"login": "AbdelrhmanBassiouny"}, "body": "The names you have chosen are so specific that nothing no rule will ever fit except the current role you should choose names that are as general as possible while at the same time not so general that it's not related to rules at all but as general as possible to allow for extra rules to be added to that section and I think for example here it's related to generics how to use generics with data classes and for the others for example serialization in general doesn't have to be situations realization also when it comes to the path enumerations just use enums and then specify about that. \n\nHow do I think we are limited on the naming because this is the name of the section but it's the same time the name of the topic what if there is a topic that can be across can be the same across sections and that can happen we can talk about exceptions in krrood rules and at the same time exceptions in Python rules so we need to find a way to save the topic without having it to be colliding with the section name. ", "createdAt": "2026-10-27T17:19:10Z", "url": "https://github.com/cram2/cognitive_robot_abstract_machine/pull/806#discussion_r4391885993"}]}}]}}}}}], "job_logs": []}
